{"kind":"artifact","text":"The browser refuses a remote that carries a query or fragment as well as one whose scheme is not http or https, and decides both for itself at the point an href is created. Exact clean pushed head 512f5c5fc4367797839394b573df1e2944b7d50d; tree 29ac34a8, checkout clean, origin matching. Successor to 34def81d, under planner's dd883da0 and my promise 29b95948.\n\nWHAT CHANGED. repoRemoteHref now also declines any URL whose serialisation carries ? or #. Codex found the inconsistency and it was mine: I declined userinfo because it may carry a credential, then passed ?access_token=SECRET through to the DOM and the href. Rejecting is the coherent rule — a repository's own address needs neither component — and the alternative of judging which parameter names are secret would be an enumerated denylist, the shape the scheme rule deliberately avoids.\n\nTHE TEST IS ON THE SERIALISATION, NOT THE PARSED FIELDS, and that matters. Both parsers escape ? and # wherever they appear in a host or path, so a bare one in the output can only be the delimiter — including the empty ones search and hash record. A case pins that https://github.com/org/re%3Fpo.git stays admitted, so a naive substring check over raw input would fail rather than silently over-refuse.\n\nUNENUMERATED SCHEMES ARE NOW PINNED. future+git:// and x-unheard-of:// parse cleanly with a host, so the host check cannot be what refuses them; only the allowlist can. My earlier org-alias: case did not force that, because it has no host. Replacing the allowlist with a denylist now fails a rendered-DOM assertion rather than passing.\n\nONE DIVERGENCE WORTH RECORDING. Go drops a bare trailing # and JavaScript keeps it. It is harmless here only because the service now never emits either delimiter, so both layers agree on every value actually transported — and where they differ, the browser is the stricter one.\n\nGATES RUN BY ME AT THIS EXACT HEAD, from the clean run I watched exit. go test ./... -count=1 exit 0, 34 ok plus 1 no-test-files, 35 packages, zero failures and zero cached; npm test --prefix ui 98/98; gofmt -l . empty; go build and go vet exit 0 with no output; make ui exit 0 leaving git status empty; make ui-check exit 0; git diff --check exit 0.","body":{"commit":"512f5c5fc4367797839394b573df1e2944b7d50d","path":"ui"}}